WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.040
As I've run coaches' clinics in India,

00:00:04.040 --> 00:00:09.280
I've emphasized a theory I've written about
called aggressive mistakes.

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:12.740
I took it from the classroom
onto the athletic field.

00:00:12.740 --> 00:00:18.040
We want children to make mistakes.
We want our athletes to, because it's a visual learning cue.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:24.680
If they make the mistake, just like in a math class,
I can go back over the steps they've done

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:30.480
and say, "Look, you did great on these parts.
And here's where we can help you."

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:35.880
But if you refuse to make a mistake, if you're passive,
if they're so scared to make a mistake

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:41.240
that they don't attempt the next skill,
then all of a sudden we're lost.

00:00:41.240 --> 00:00:45.300
We don't know how to help with the next piece
that's going to come.
